WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.200
For forty years, KRAS was called undruggable — the protein behind a quarter of all human cancers.

2
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:13.700
It was finally beaten not through its active site, but through a hidden pocket in its shape — encoded in contact topology.

3
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:23.100
So we gave that shape to a quantum computer. Twenty qubits. IBM's ibm_fez. Real hardware — not a simulation.

4
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:34.400
The chip kept the protein's structure — but it lost its direction. And you can hear the difference. Each edge is a note. That's the emulator.

5
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:42.500
[emulator sonification — each graph edge, one note]

6
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:43.900
That's the chip.

7
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:51.400
[ibm_fez sonification — same graph, real silicon]

8
00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:02.200
If hardware can feel the shape of a protein, drug discovery might someday run on physics itself. Every claim links to a raw job receipt. This is the Kytos Observatory.
